:: Beach Comb
<<effects>>
The tide is out. You walk along the waterline, picking through what the sea left behind. Seaweed, driftwood, broken shells.
<<set _combRoll to random(1, 100)>>
<<if _combRoll lte 5>>
	Something dark and round rests in the sand. You pick it up. <span class="blue">A black pearl.</span> It's cool to the touch, and heavier than it looks.
	<br>
	<span class="navy"><<if $waterdragonbuild gte 1>>You feel a strong urge to swallow it.<<else>>It looks as if it held the depths themselves.<</if>></span>
	<br><br>
	<<tficon "waterdragon">><<link [[Swallow it|Beach Comb Pearl Eat]]>><<transform waterdragon 5>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<highicon>><<link [[Pocket it|Beach Comb Pearl Keep]]>><<money 40000 "beachComb">><</link>>
<<elseif _combRoll lte 30>>
	A pale gleam catches your eye. You brush away the sand and find a smooth, milky stone. <span class="blue">A moonstone.</span> It glows faintly in the dark.
	<br>
	<span class="navy"><<if $waterdragonbuild gte 1>>Your mouth waters.<<else>>For some reason, you want to put it in your mouth.<</if>></span>
	<br><br>
	<<tficon "waterdragon">><<link [[Swallow it|Beach Comb Moonstone Eat]]>><<transform waterdragon 1>><</link>>
	<br>

	<<highicon>><<link [[Pocket it|Beach Comb Moonstone Keep]]>><<money 10000 "beachComb">><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<set _combLoot to random(500, 1000)>>
	You find a few coins half-buried in the sand.
	<br><br>
	You've gained <<printmoney _combLoot>>.<<money _combLoot "beachComb">>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Beach]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Beach Comb Pearl Eat
<<effects>>
You swallow the pearl before you can think better of it. It goes down cold, and a shiver runs through your body.
<<if $waterdragonbuild gte 30>><span class="gold">Where it belongs.</span><<else>><span class="gold">You don't know why you did that, but somehow it calms you down.</span><</if>><<lstress>><<stress -4>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Beach]]>><</link>>

:: Beach Comb Pearl Keep
<<effects>>

You pocket the pearl. It will sell for a good sum. <<if $waterdragonbuild gte 1>><span class="red">You can't help but feel bad about it.</span><</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>

:: Beach Comb Moonstone Eat
<<effects>>
You swallow the stone. It tastes of salt, and a coolness spreads through your chest.

<<if $waterdragonbuild gte 30>><span class="gold">Where it belongs.</span><<else>><span class="gold">You don't know why, but somehow it calms you down.</span><</if>><<lstress>><<stress -2>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>

:: Beach Comb Moonstone Keep
<<effects>>
You pocket the stone. It should fetch a decent price. <<if $waterdragonbuild gte 1>><span class="purple">Part of you doesn't want to let it go.</span><</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>


:: Water Dragon Island Travel
<<set $waterdragonJourneyDay to 1>>
<<set $sea to 100>>
<<effects>>
You slip beneath the surface and let the current take your weight. Instinct tells you this won't be a single desperate sprint. 
The pull in your chest comes and goes with the tide, drawing you onward.
<br><br>
This will take days. A week, perhaps. Long enough for the sea to wear your strength down to the bone.
<br><br>
<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Begin the crossing|Water Dragon Island Travel Day]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Water Dragon Island Travel Day
<<effects>>
<<set _travelFatigue to Math.max(8, Math.floor(C.tiredness.max * 0.08))>>
<<set $tiredness = Math.clamp($tiredness + _travelFatigue, 0, C.tiredness.max)>>
Day <<print $waterdragonJourneyDay>> of your crossing leaves your muscles aching. Salt dries tight upon your skin, and the sea seems to shift around your mood, now playful, now cold, now watchful.
<<stress 8>><<gstress>><br><br>
<<set _travelRoll to random(1, 11)>>
<<if _travelRoll is 1>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Whale 1]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _travelRoll is 2>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Dolphins]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _travelRoll is 3>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Sea Eye]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _travelRoll is 4>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Rest]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _travelRoll is 5>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Trash]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _travelRoll is 6>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Shoal]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _travelRoll is 7>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Current]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _travelRoll is 8>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Storm]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _travelRoll is 9>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Song]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _travelRoll is 10>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Black Moon]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Blood Moon]]>><</link>>
<</if>>


:: Water Dragon Travel Whale 1
<<effects>>
The water beneath you turns abruptly cold. A shadow vast enough to swallow your whole body glides below, then rises. 
A whale breaches beside you in a crashing wall of foam, its cry rolling through your ribs like thunder.
<br><br>
Every instinct in your body flares. You bare your teeth and surge toward it rather than away.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Whale 2]]>><</link>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Whale 2
<<effects>>
You strike first. Claws, horns, tail, whatever your changed body can bring to bear, you throw all of it into the fight. 
Spray and bloodless white foam explode around you as the whale turns, forcing you into a spinning dance of brute mass and furious agility.
<br><br>
It is magnificent. It is also pointless. The beast is too large, too old, and the sea itself seems to move with it.
<br><br>
Still, you refuse to retreat until the shape of that truth settles in your chest.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Whale 3]]>><</link>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Whale 3
<<effects>>
You stop striking and open your mouth on a ragged breath. What comes out isn't any language you know. 
It spills from somewhere older and deeper, a vibrating trill threaded with strange clicks and resonant notes.
<br><br>
You don't understand what you're saying. Somehow, the whale does.
<br><br>
It circles once, enormous eye fixed on you, then lets out a low call that shivers through the water and dives back into the dark. 
The pressure of its passing nearly flips you over, but when the sea calms again, you realise it chose to leave you be.<<gawareness>><<awareness 1>>
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Dolphins
<<effects>><<beastNEWinit 3 dolphin>>
A pod of dolphins cuts through the swells toward you, accompanied by their stranger kin. 
The dolphins chatter in bright, breathy bursts, and before long the whole group is circling you in delighted loops, bumping your hips and shoulders as if asking you to join their game.
<br><br>
For a little while, the crossing stops being a trial and becomes play.
<br><br>
<<if hasSexStat("deviancy", 3, true) and (($monster is 1 or $settings.bestialityEnabled) and not ($NPCList[0] and $NPCList[0].lewdBlocked))>>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Play with them|Water Dragon Travel Dolphins Friendly]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Play a little too intimately|Sea Dolphins Sex]]>>
		<<set $waterdragonJourneySex to 1>><<set $sexstart to 1>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>><<deviant3>>
<<else>>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Play with them|Water Dragon Travel Dolphins Friendly]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Dolphins Friendly
<<effects>>
You spin and dive with the pod until laughter leaves you breathless. The dolphins leap around you, splash you in the face, and veer away only when the current changes.
The sea feels a little less lonely after they go.<<lstress>><<stress -10>>
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Sea Eye
<<effects>>
Something glimmers far below you. Not threatening, not even clear, just a distant suggestion of a shape that makes your whole body tense with recognition.
<br><br>
Instead of dread, a fierce urge takes hold. You dive.
<br><br>
Down and down you go, chasing that impossible glint through the green dark, only to find nothing but the slow sway of weeds and the vast, aching beauty of the sea. 
When you surface again, your throat is tight with a sadness you can't explain as if you had almost found a memory and lost it again.<<ltrauma>><<trauma -2>>
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Rest
<<effects>>
You find a flat black rock jutting from the sea, warm where it has held the day's light of the sun. You drag yourself onto it and lie there for a while as gulls wheel overhead, their cries sharp and clean in the wind.
<br><br>
The view is beautiful. For a few precious minutes, nothing hunts you and nothing asks anything of you.<<lstress>><<stress -6>><<ltrauma>><<trauma -1>>
<<set _restGain to Math.max(6, Math.floor(C.tiredness.max * 0.05))>>
<<set $tiredness = Math.clamp($tiredness - _restGain, 0, C.tiredness.max)>>
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Trash
<<effects>>
A discarded skein of netting drifts beneath the chop. You don't notice it until it snares your limbs and tail, dragging garbage and hooks against your body as the current twists everything tighter.
<br><br>
It takes long, furious effort to tear yourself free. When you finally do, the sea around you is flecked with bits of floating rubbish that should never have been there at all.<<ggstress>><<stress 28>>
<br><br>
The sight of the trash in the sea leaves a bitter weight in your chest.
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Shoal
<<effects>>
A silver shoal of fish flashes around you like living moonlight. Instinct takes over. You dart after it, body moving with sudden, easy precision, and snatch enough fish to quiet the ache in your belly before the school scatters.
<<lstress>><<stress -14>>
<br><br>
The hunt leaves you feeling sharp, sleek, and alive.
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Current
<<effects>>
You drift into a warm current thick with glowing plankton. Every sweep of your limbs scatters cold stars through the water around you and for a while you swim through your own private sky.
<br><br>
The sight coaxes an answering trill from your throat before you can stop it. The sound feels right.
<br><br>
Familiar, even.<<lstress>><<stress -8>><<gawareness>><<awareness 1>>
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Storm
<<effects>>
A storm catches you without warning. Waves rear around you like walls and you spend what feels like hours climbing one collapsing crest after another. More than once you nearly lose the surface entirely.<<gstress>><<stress 6>>
<br><br>
Yet somewhere amid the terror, exhilaration sparks. You are small beside the storm, but you are still here, still moving, still answering the sea with your own stubborn strength.
<br><br>
<<set _stormFatigue to Math.max(4, Math.floor(C.tiredness.max * 0.04))>>
<<set $tiredness = Math.clamp($tiredness + _stormFatigue, 0, C.tiredness.max)>>
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Song
<<effects>>
You hear singing carried oddly across the water. There is no ship in sight, no shore, no visible singer. Still, the sound coils through your chest and draws a quiet answer from you, a chirr and warbling note you didn't know you could make.
<br><br>
When the song fades, you are alone again, but less lonely than before.<<lstress>><<stress -4>><<if $islander_language isnot undefined>><<islander_language 10>><<gcomprehension>><</if>>
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Black Moon
<<effects>>
You pause, one hand lifted from the surface.
<br><br>
Nothing has changed. The same sea, the same sky, the same distant smudge of the island behind you. And yet something presses at the edge of your thoughts so faint and far away it might belong to another world entirely.
<br><br>
Another moon.
<br><br>
The idea is ridiculous. You're not looking at any moon. You don't know why your mind went there. Still, the name surfaces as though it's been sitting quietly at the back of your throat. <span class="navy">a black moon, yet feels so bright</span>.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Black Moon 2]]>><</link>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Black Moon 2
<<effects>>
How can black be bright? How can something with no light pull at you like a beacon? The question holds for only a moment before the memory moves over it like a wave.
<br><br>
It was bright because <i>they</i> knew it. Because <i>they</i> watched for it. Under that impossible moon, the deep didn't feel empty.
<br><br>
For a moment the water around you feels crowded with the memory of <i>them</i>. Long shapes through silver-dark water. Hands finding hands beneath the tide. One of them surfacing near the rocks, speaking the island tongue badly while a human laughs and corrects them. <i>They</i> tries again, quieter this time. The human smiles.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Black Moon 3]]>><</link>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Black Moon 3
<<effects>>
The warmth of it makes your chest ache.
<br><br>
Then the memory thins. The sea is only the sea again.
<br><br>
Why did that come to you? History? Instinct? Something the transformation dredged up from a shape you were never meant to carry?
<br><br>
<<if $waterdragonbuild gte 30>>
	The longing hurts, but it fits somehow as your tail moving through the water, something in you still recognising what it means to belong to a people.<<llstress>><<stress -10>><<ltrauma>><<trauma -2>>
<<else>>
	You shake it off and keep swimming. The ache stays, like a song half-remembered on waking. Whatever you're becoming, it seems to know more than you do.<<lstress>><<stress -4>>
<</if>><<if $islander_language isnot undefined>><<islander_language 5>><<gcomprehension>><</if>>
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Blood Moon
<<effects>>
You stop so sharply the water closes over your shoulders.
Something is wrong. A colour blooms behind your eyes, as though something on the far side of the world has turned to look at you. Another moon. Your body understands the omen before your mind catches up.
<br><br>
<span class="navy">Blood Moon.</span>
<br><br>
The name is familiar. Yet this blood moon lands in your thoughts with the weight of something older. A warning carved into bone, maybe. A word remembered by flesh that should not remember anything.
<br><br>
Is this the same blood moon people sometimes glimpse without understanding? Is this truly the blood moon you know, or is your mind forcing a familiar name onto something far older?
Either way... why are you afraid?
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Blood Moon 2]]>><</link>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Blood Moon 2
<<effects>>
It comes in pieces.
<br><br>
Children tucked into hollows beneath the reef. Fires smothered before the smoke could rise. Warriors moving through black water without a sound, eyes fixed on the dark beyond the tribe's edge.
<br><br>
Blood moon was not a celebration. It was the time to disappear.
<br><br>
That bothers you. You know how easily people explain the blood moon away as something that make the sky red, a rough night, someone acting strangely and blaming the time. 
But the fear moving through you now doesn't feel like that. It doesn't feel learned from rumour or monthly warnings or anything you picked up on land.
<br><br>
It feels inherited. As though something beneath the sea had already named it long before you ever saw it rise above a rooftop.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Travel Blood Moon 3]]>><</link>>

:: Water Dragon Travel Blood Moon 3
<<effects>>
For an instant, the danger is no longer only the ancient red omen. It becomes betrayal. 
<br><br>
The memory shows <i>them</i> listening from beneath the rocks, learning the human's words with hopeful hearts. Then those same voices turned against them.
<i>Their</i> homes ended up being left behind. Kin scattered into the open ocean. Far behind <i>them</i>, something vast moved through the dark, following until even <i>their</i> speed could not save <i>them</i>. 
<br><br>
You blink, and it's gone.
<br><br>
The island is still there. The sea is still flat. Then what was that? A legend? A warning? A dead people's grief working its way up through your changing body? Or did the blood moon always mean more than most people were able to see?
<br><br>
<<if $waterdragonbuild gte 30>>
	Fear moves through you but so does something steadier: a recognition. Your body knowing the shape of an old warrior's calm. You let it carry you and keep swimming away.<<gstress>><<stress 6>><<gawareness>><<awareness 1>>
<<else>>
	You duck beneath a mat of weed and press your claws into the rock until the feeling passes. When you surface, your limbs are stiff and the old terror is still there, clinging.<<gggstress>><<stress 14>>
	<<set _bloodMoonFatigue to Math.max(4, Math.floor(C.tiredness.max * 0.03))>><<set $tiredness = Math.clamp($tiredness + _bloodMoonFatigue, 0, C.tiredness.max)>><<ggtiredness>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<waterdragonTravelContinue>>

:: Water Dragon Island Arrival 1
<<effects>>
The pull that has been bringing you here grows stronger, no longer a distant ache but a deep, steady tug beneath your ribs. By now you are so tired the sea seems to move you more than you move yourself.
<br><br>
Then, through rain-mist and spray, an island rises ahead.
<br><br>
It feels familiar. 
<<if $spear_vessel>>
	You know you've set foot here before, and yet some buried part of you also knows the familiar feeling isn't from that.
<<else>>
	You know with perfect certainty that you have never seen it before and yet some buried part of you knows it all the same.
<</if>><br><br>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Island Arrival 2]]>><</link>>

:: Water Dragon Island Arrival 2
<<effects>>
You force yourself through the final stretch. Pebbled sand grinds beneath your palms when at last you reach the shallows, and you drag yourself higher as each receding wave tries to claim you back.
<br><br>
The scent of flowers catches in your nose. Your ears twitch toward distant cries in the trees. Everything feels too vivid, as if the island has been waiting for you to notice it properly.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Island Arrival 3]]>><</link>>

:: Water Dragon Island Arrival 3
<<effects>>
You rise unsteadily onto your feet. Your tail swishes behind you of its own accord, and a loud, bright chirping trill bursts out of your throat before you can stop it.
<br><br>
You freeze, startled. You didn't even know you could make a sound like that.
<br><br>
Excitement follows the shock almost immediately. Exhausted as you are, something in you is eager to explore.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Water Dragon Island Arrival 4]]>><</link>>

:: Water Dragon Island Arrival 4
<<effects>>
<<set _arrivalFatigue to Math.max(6, Math.floor(C.tiredness.max * 0.05))>>
<<set $tiredness = Math.clamp($tiredness + _arrivalFatigue, 0, C.tiredness.max)>>
Whether the island is truly calling you or you have simply gone half feral with fatigue, you can't say. All you know is that some deep, wordless part of you feels safer here than it has any right to.
<<lstress>><<stress -4>><<ltrauma>><<trauma -1>><br><br>
<<set $waterdragonJourneyDay to 0>>
<<set $sea to 0>>
<<set $location to "island">>
<<updatesidebarimg>>
<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Step onto the beach|Island Beach]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Whitney Water Dragon
<<effects>>
You draw a breath and let out a sudden, strange, warbling squeak clawing its way up your throat before you can stop it.
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Whitney.love gte 15 and $loft_whitney gte 6>>
	/* Tier 3: high love + deep-bond event */
	Whitney is caught entirely off guard. <<His>> eyes go wide,
	and before <<he>> can think better of it <<he>> lets out a loud, highly uncharacteristic scream right back at you.
	<br><br>
	For a heartbeat the two of you just stare at each other, equally startled by the noise <<he>> just made.
	<<if !$daily.whitney.waterDragon>>
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Shriek louder|Whitney Water Dragon Shriek]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<He>> clears <<his>> throat and looks pointedly out at nothing, pretending it never happened.
		"Say a word about that and you're dead, slut."
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<whitneyoptions>>
<<elseif C.npc.Whitney.dom gte 20 and C.npc.Whitney.love lte 10>>
	/* Tier 1: low love / high dom, no reward (not farmable) */
	Whitney flinches hard, <<his>> face twisting into an immediate scowl.
	<<He>> doesn't wait for an explanation as <<he>> lashes out and shoves you back with a sharp kick.
	<br><br>
	"What the fuck was that?!" <<His>> face is twisted in disgust.
	"You are so fuckin' noisy! Piss off, weirdo, before I give you a real reason to squeal."
	<<pain 4>><<gpain>><<stress 6>><<gstress>>
	<br><br>
	<<if $location is "park" and Weather.precipitation isnot "none">>
		You stumble back into the grass, the <<print Weather.precipitation>> soaking through your clothes.
		<<wet_all>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	You back off before <<he>> decides to make good on the threat.
	<br><br>
	<<whitneyexit>>
<<else>>
	/* Tier 2: ordinary / high-ish love */
	<<if !$daily.whitney.waterDragon>>
		<<set $daily.whitney.waterDragon to true>>
		Whitney visibly jumps, genuinely startled to the point
		<<if $whitney_smoke isnot undefined and !playerBellyVisible()>>
			the cigarette nearly tumbles from <<his>> lips before <<he>> snatches it back.
		<<else>>
			<<he>> stumbles half a step before catching <<his>> balance.
		<</if>>
		<<He>> recovers fast, scrambling to save face.
		<br><br>
		"Fuckin' hell, warn a person, will you?" <<he>> mutters, rubbing the back of <<his>> neck. 
		"You're a total freak, slut. Just... keep that weird racket down next time."
		<<npcincr Whitney love 1>><<glove>>
		<br><br>
		<<whitneyoptions>>
	<<else>>
		Whitney's heard it once already today, and <<his>> patience is gone. <<He>> rounds on you with a hiss, lip curling.
		<br><br>
		<<set _shoveChance to random(1, 100)>>
		<<if $location is "park" and _shoveChance lt 35>>
			"Are you fuckin' kidding me? Again?"
			<<athleticsdifficulty 650 1000 true>>
			Before you can react, Whitney grabs you and starts hauling you towards the fountain.
			<<if $athleticsSuccess>>
				<span class="green">You steady yourself,</span> boots dragging in the dirt, and stop <<him>> from dunking you.
				<<He>> gives you one last frustrated pull before letting go.
				<br><br>
				"You're no fun." <<He>> stalks back to <<his>> spot under the tree.
				<br><br>
				<<whitneyoptions>>
			<<else>>
				You <span class="red">trip, and <<he>> shoves you over the edge.</span>
				You go straight in<<if Time.season is "winter">>, cracking through the thin ice and<</if>> come up drenched.
				<<wet_all>>
				<br><br>
				"You know what? Feel loads better now. Cheers, <<bitch>>."
				<<He>> leaves you floundering in the fountain, laughing as <<he>> walks off out of the park.
				<br><br>
				<<whitneyexit>>
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			"Pack it in, slut, you're givin' me a headache." <<He>> jabs a finger at your chest.
			"One more peep and I'll give you somethin' to actually squeal about."
			<br><br>
			<<whitneyoptions>>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Whitney Water Dragon Shriek
<<effects>>
You puff up your chest and shriek even louder.
<br><br>
Not to be outdone, Whitney's eyes go wide and <<he>> screams right back in your face. 
For a few absurd seconds the two of you are locked in a deafening, ridiculous shouting match<<if $location is "park">> that people across the park turn to stare<</if>>.
<br><br>
Then Whitney breaks. <<His>> scream cracks into a snort, and <<he>> doubles over, laughing harder than you've ever seen <<him>> laugh. 
<br><br>
"Holy shit!" <<he>> wheezes, shoving your shoulder. "You are such a fucking weirdo. What is wrong with you?!"
<<set $daily.whitney.waterDragon to true>>
<<stress -10>><<lllstress>>
<<npcincr Whitney love 3>><<glove>>
<br><br>
<<whitneyexit>>

/*
	=====================================================================
	 WATER DRAGON TF; ISLAND DEFEAT BYPASS & ELDER ENCOUNTER
	=====================================================================

	HOW IT FLOWS:
	  count 0 	 -> Awe. Ritual abandoned, PC released untouched.
	  count 1 	 -> Breeding attempt (narrative -> combat -> narrative).
	  count 5+ 	 -> Breeding begins, Elder interrupts, lore, Elder leads PC to the spear chamber
	  more else	 -> Elder calls PC directly (social visit)

	VARIABLES ADDED (can be used for future events if want):
	  $island.dragon_defeat_count   — progression counter
	  $island.dragon_elder_met      — unlocks recurring Elder visits
	=====================================================================
*/
/* FIRST DEFEAT (no breeding, PC released) */
:: Island Defeat Dragon Awe
<<effects>>
<<generateRole 2 0 "islander">><<person3>>
A courtyard echoes with the rumble of unseen drums. The islanders smack their thighs and chests in time with the sound, as a <<person>> advances on you with round mask, three small circles above the eyes and mouth, a bundle of thin leaves in one hand, an ivory knife in the other.
<br><br>
<<He>> raises the knife. Traces it along your collarbone, over your shoulder, down to where the skin gives way to <span class="navy">scales.</span>
<br><br>
The knife stops. The <<persons>> hand trembles. <<He>> pulls the blade back, steps away from you, and for a long moment simply... stares.
<br><br>
The drums falter. One by one, the rhythms fall out of time with each other, then out of time altogether, until the courtyard holds only the sound of wind and breath. A murmur moves through the crowd.
<br><br>
<<if $islander_language gte 100>>
	"...scales..."
	<br>
	"...impossible. It's impossible..."
	<br>
	"...look, look at <<phim>>..."
	<br>
	"...the old ones... the lost kin..."
<<elseif $islander_language gte 50>>
	You catch fragments — words like "scales," "impossible," "old ones," "lost" — passing from mouth to mouth beneath the masks.
<<else>>
	They whisper in their incomprehensible language, but you recognise the shape of the sound. Awe. Or something like fear.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Island Defeat Dragon Awe 2]]>><</link>>

:: Island Defeat Dragon Awe 2
<<effects>>
The <<person3>><<person>> drops the bundle of leaves. The knife follows, clattering against the stone. <<He>> sinks to <<his>> knees, and presses <<his>> forehead to the ground in front of you.
<br><br>
Another follows. 
<br><br>
Then another.
<br><br>
The <<person1>><<person>> and <<person2>><<person>> exchange a look above their masks. Hesitantly, they loosen the ropes binding you to the stick. 
Hands steady you, some lingering a moment too long on your scales as if trying to prove to themselves that you're real.
<br><br>
No one speaks directly to you. They back away, heads lowered, and leave a path clear to the arch at the edge of the courtyard.
<br><br>
You're free.
<br><br>
<<unbind>><<leg_unbind>>
<<link [[Walk out|Island Defeat Dragon Released]]>><</link>>

:: Island Defeat Dragon Released
<<effects>>
You walk past the kneeling islanders. None of them lift their heads. The one who was going to carve you with a plant still shakes, staring at the stones beneath <<his>> palms.
<br><br>
The corridor leads you back out into the woods.
<br><br>
You hear the drums start again somewhere behind you as you walk away.
<br><br>
<<set $island.dragon_defeat_count to 1>>
<<if !$island.home>>
	<<link [[Next|Island Treeline Search]]>><<endcombat>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Island]]>><<endcombat>><</link>>
<</if>>

/* BREEDING ATTEMPT (narrative -> combat -> narrative) */
:: Island Defeat Dragon Breed Intro
<<effects>>
<<generateRole 2 0 "islander">><<generateRole 3 0 "islander">><<person3>>
The drums don't start. That is the first thing you notice.
<br><br>
No masked person steps forward with leaves and a knife. Instead, the crowd shifts. Murmurs pass through it with something lower and hungrier. A group of <<personsimple>>s steps out from the front of the line, and the higher-ranked islanders around them
<<if $islander_language gte 100>>
	glance at each other. "Again," one mutters. "They're going to try again."
	<br>
	"Let them. It is our shame to bear. Our debt."
<<elseif $islander_language gte 50>>
	speak in low tones. You catch the word of shame, and debt, repeated.
<<else>>
	exchange words in their incomprehensible language.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<person3>>
The <<person>> in front steps closer. <<He>> doesn't lift a knife. <<His>> hand shakes as <<he>> presses it flat against the scales on your shoulder.
<br><br>
<<if $islander_language gte 100>>
	"Forgive us," <<he>> breathes, barely audible beneath the mask. "Forgive us. We have to. <span class="pink">We have to bring them back.</span>"
<<elseif $islander_language gte 50>>
	<<He>> whispers something under the mask. You catch forgive, and bring them back.
<<else>>
	<<He>> whispers in their tongue. You don't understand the words, but the cadence is a plea.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Island Defeat Dragon Breed]]>><<set $molestationstart to 1>><</link>>

:: Island Defeat Dragon Breed
<<if $molestationstart is 1>>
	<<set $molestationstart to 0>>
	<<controlloss>>
	<<violence 1>>
	<<neutral 1>>
	<<molested>>
	<<maninit>>
<</if>>
<<effects>>
<<effectsman>>
<<alarmstate>>
<<man>>
<<stateman>>
<br><br>
<<actionsman>>
<<if _combatend>>
	<<if $island.dragon_defeat_count gte 5 and !$island.dragon_elder_met>>
		<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Island Defeat Dragon Intervene]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
	<<else>>
		<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Island Defeat Dragon Breed Finish]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Island Defeat Dragon Breed]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<</if>>

:: Island Defeat Dragon Breed Finish
<<effects>>
<<if $enemyhealth lte 0>>
	The <<person>> reels back, beaten. The others hesitate. And in their hesitation, you manage to pull free.
	<br><br>
<<else>>
	<<ejaculation>>
	The <<person>> withdraws, head bowed, and backs away from you with both hands raised as though in apology.
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<if $islander_language gte 100>>
	"It isn't working," someone whispers at the edge of the crowd.
	<br>
	"Of course it isn't. We are not the ones meant to do this."
	<br>
	"Then why do we keep—"
	<br>
	"<i>Because we owe them</i>."
<<elseif $islander_language gte 50>>
	Whispers travel the crowd. You think you hear the word <i>owe</i>.
<<else>>
	They murmur amongst themselves in their tongue. You don't need to understand them to hear the weariness in it.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Island Defeat Dragon Breed Finish 2]]>><</link>>

:: Island Defeat Dragon Breed Finish 2
<<effects>>
The islanders carry you from the ruins, back to the rapid river bridged by a log. They haul the stick back into an upright position, so that you face the edge of the river.
<br><br>
With a single movement, the <<person>> slices through all the bindings attaching you to the rope. You plunge into the river.
<br><br>
You fall.
<br><br>
<<set $island.dragon_defeat_count += 1>>
<<unbind>><<leg_unbind>>
<<link [[Next|Island Defeat Tattoo End 2]]>><<endcombat>><</link>>

/* ELDER INTERVENTION (triggers on the 5th dragon defeat) */
:: Island Defeat Dragon Intervene
<<effects>>
<<generateRole 4 0 "old islander">><<saveNPC 4 "waterdragon_elder">><<person5>>
The <<person3>><<person>> is still before you, breath ragged when the courtyard goes quiet.
<br><br>
It isn't the quiet of the drums stopping because the drums weren't even being played. This is the quiet of a room when somebody senior walks in.
<br><br>
A <<person5>><<personsimple>> in a hooded robe steps out from the shadow of the arch. <<He>> wears no mask. 
The islanders part for <<him>> without being asked; the masked ones, the ones currently crowding you. <<His>> eyes are the only thing in the courtyard that seems older than the stones.
<br><br>
<<He>> looks at the <<person3>><<person>>. <<He>> does not raise <<his>> voice when talking.
<<if $islander_language gte 100>>
	"Enough."
	<br><br>
	The <<person3>><<person>> flinches as if struck.
	<br><br>
	"Untie the vessel. Step away. All of you."
<<elseif $islander_language gte 50>>
	A single word. You understand the shape of it as an order.
	<br><br>
	The <<person3>><<person>> flinches. Another word, something about untying.
<<else>>
	A single word in the old tongue. You don't understand it, but the <<person3>><<person>> flinches as if struck. Another word. Hands fumble to obey.
<</if>>
<br><br>
The ropes loosen. The crowd backs away, heads lowered, some of them whispering what might be apologies as they retreat.
<br><br>
The hooded <<person5>><<personsimple>> looks at you for the first time. <<His>> expression doesn't change. <<He>> lifts one hand and tilts <<his>> head toward the corridor <<he>> came from.
<br><br>
<i>Which means follow.</i>
<br><br>
<<unbind>><<leg_unbind>>
<<link [[Follow|Island Defeat Dragon Follow]]>><<endcombat>><</link>>

:: Island Defeat Dragon Follow
<<effects>>
<<loadNPC 0 "waterdragon_elder">><<person1>>
You follow the <<personsimple>> through corridors you weren't carried through. These are older than the rest of the ruined walls that were fitted stone before the castle above them fell, floors polished by centuries of bare feet.
<br><br>
The <<person>> doesn't speak. <<His>> robe carries over the stone. Torches in brackets flare as you pass them, then gutter low again behind you, as though the light itself is reluctant to linger.
<br><br>
At a heavy wooden door, <<he>> stops. <<He>> places <<his>> palm against it, and the door swings inward on its own.
<br><br>
<<link [[Enter|Islander Elder Meeting]]>><</link>>

:: Islander Elder Meeting
<<effects>>
The room beyond is round, low-ceilinged, carved out of the same polished stone. A brazier burns in the centre. Shelves line the walls with scrolls, jars, carved figurines, things you don't have names for. The air smells of salt and old smoke.
<<He>> sets a kettle onto a hook above the flame.
<br><br>
Two other masked islanders stand just inside the door. A third is tending the fire. None of them look at you directly. They look at <<him>>, as if waiting.
<br><br>
"Leave us," <<he>> says.
<br><br>
The masked ones leave without a word. The door closes behind them on its own, the same way it opened. The brazier crackles.
<br><br>
The <<person>> finally turns to face you.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Islander Elder Alone]]>><</link>>

:: Islander Elder Alone
<<effects>>
"Forgive them. They were not cruel to you. Only..." <<person>> searches for the word, "desperate. In a way that has had nowhere to go for a very long time."
<br><br>
<<He>> gestures for you to sit. A low stone bench appears to have been there the whole time. You're not certain it was.
<br><br>
"Please. Sit. You are the first of your kind to walk through that door in—" <<he>> stops, considers, and something briefly crosses <<his>> face that might be grief or might be a smile. "In a length of time."
<br><br>
<<link [[Sit|Islander Elder Lore]]>><</link>>

:: Islander Elder Lore
<<effects>><<wearProp "tea">>
You sit. The <<person>> pours a thin, pale tea from the kettle, and hands you a cup. It smells faintly of brine and flowers.
<br><br>
"I will not pretend I don't know what you are," <<he>> says, settling onto the stones opposite you. "The scales. The way the light bends around you in water, even here, where you are dry. <i>One of the old ones</i>."
<br><br>
<<He>> cradles <<his>> own cup. Doesn't drink.
<br><br>
"They were not born of this sea. They came from waters half a world away, warm seas to the far southeast, whose true names our oldest scrolls only guess at. They lived there beside humans long enough that neither remembered a time before the other."
<br><br>
<<He>> watches the brazier for a moment.
<br><br>
"Then one of them was taken. Corrupted, by the thing the deep scrolls call Auriga. Its scales turned the dark purple of a drowned sky, and horns grew from its head like those of a great elk.
Your people gave the corrupted one a name: <span class="purple">Bakunawa</span>. Before the old ones saved it."
<br><br>
<<link [[Listen|Islander Elder Lore 2]]>><</link>>

:: Islander Elder Lore 2
<<effects>><<wearProp "tea">>
"The humans of their home waters did not thank the old ones," <<he>> continues. "They saw only what one dragon had done, and what any dragon might do. Fear won, as it often does. The old ones were driven from the seas that had borne them."
<br><br>
"Displaced, they crossed open ocean until they found this place, and settled on it and beneath it. They gave the island the name it still carries in our records. Parusa. In their tongue, and now in ours: punishment. They believed exile was the sentence for what one of their own had become."
<br><br>
"Before the first humans crossed this sea, they were here. They built nothing and needed to build nothing. The tide was their house and the reef was their garden.
They sang to each other across distances that would break your ears to hear." <<He>> pauses. "They were beautiful."
<br><br>
"Then our ancestors came. Exiles too, in their own way. But they did not fear the old ones. They were curious. They taught the dragons their words, and the dragons taught them the sea's words in return. A union of land and water. And then..."
<br><br>
<<He>> looks down at the tea.
<br><br>
"So. You can imagine what it did to the islanders when you stepped onto their stones with <i>scales</i>. The first of the old ones alive in living memory. What they did to you... I know. I should have come sooner. I am sorry."
<br><br>
<<link [[Listen|Islander Elder Lore 3]]>><</link>>

:: Islander Elder Lore 3
<<effects>><<wearProp "tea">>
<<He>> finally drinks. Sets the cup down.
"So. You can imagine what it did to the islanders when you stepped onto their stones with <i>scales</i>. What they did to you... I know. I should have come sooner. I am sorry."
<br><br>
<<He>> shakes <<his>> head.
<br><br>
"What they're trying to do is good, in the only way they know how. They want the old ones back. They want to look at the sea again without flinching.
But it is good in a twisted shape that hurts. They have been trying to make the shame smaller by moving quickly, and their mistakes have grown impulsive."
<br><br>
<<He>> looks at you. "I should have stopped them earlier. I have stopped them now. It may not happen the same way again, if you return here."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Islander Elder Final]]>><</link>>

:: Islander Elder Final
<<effects>><<wearProp "tea">>
"Do you understand these?" <<he>> asks.
<br><br>
But <<he>> doesn't wait for an answer.
<br><br>
"You don't. This isn't about me, anyway. Or us. I know why you're here. I've been waiting. Come."
<br><br>
<<He>> sets the cup aside. Stands. Lifts a torch from a bracket on the wall. The brazier dims as the torch flares.
<br><br>
<<set $island.dragon_elder_met to true>>
<<set $island.dragon_defeat_count += 1>>
<<link [[Follow|Islander Elder Spear Intro]]>><</link>>

/* SPEAR CHAMBER */
:: Islander Elder Spear Intro
<<effects>>
A door you hadn't seen opens at a touch of the <<persons>> palm, behind one of the shelves. The passage beyond is narrower than the corridor you came through, and the stone is older still.
<br><br>
You walk. The <<person>> is silent. The path takes you by other passages. You spy a room of sorts, with a bed, another with a table, and another with what looks like an archaic musical instrument sat beside a cushion. The cave walls look natural, though scrapes and scratches suggest there have been occupants for a while.
<br><br>
You arrive at a narrow staircase, a sheer drop on either side. 
<br><br>
"Watch your step," the <<person>> says. "It isn't far."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Islander Elder Spear]]>><</link>>

:: Islander Elder Spear
<<effects>><<person1>>
<<set _generate_victim to 1>><<generateRole 1 0 "sleeper">><<saveNPC 1 "sleeper">>
At last, you arrive at even ground. The dark seems to press in, preventing the <<persons>> torchlight from reaching more than a dozen feet in any direction, but <<his>> steps are assured.
<br><br>
"Sire," <<he>> says, coming to a halt beside a brazier. You can't see who <<he>> addresses, until <<he>> shoves the torch into the vessel beside <<him>>. 
The firelight illuminates a <<person2>><<personsimple>>, lying still as a statue, arms clasped at <<his>> breast above the hilt of a gigantic, gilded spear.
<br><br>
As you look closer, you notice the figure's chest rising and falling, as if asleep.
<br><br>
"The time has come again," the <<person1>><<person>> says, softer than the old words of the ritual. "Your champion needs your spear. And this one..." <<he>> glances at you, "is of older kin than your champion. Forgive us this intrusion, and all that came before it."
<br><br>
<<He>> nods at you, and waits.
<br><br>
<<link [[Walk up to the sleeping figure|Islander Walk]]>><<set $island.walk to 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Kneel|Islander Kneel]]>><<set $island.kneel to 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Take the Spear|Islander Spear]]>><</link>>

/* POST-ELDER: PC is handed straight to the Elder, no breeding */
:: Island Defeat Dragon Elder Call
<<effects>>
<<loadNPC 4 "waterdragon_elder">><<person5>>
The masked islanders don't even try, this time. The <<person1>><<person>> and <<person2>><<person>> glance at each other as they set you upright and then look past you, to the arch.
<br><br>
<<person5>><<He>> is already there. The hooded <<personsimple>>, the Elder. <<He>> must have been told the moment you were taken. <<He>> lifts one hand. The crowd parts without a sound.
<br><br>
"Come," <<he>> says simply. "The tea is already on."
<br><br>
<<unbind>><<leg_unbind>>
<<link [[Follow|Islander Elder Revisit]]>><<endcombat>><</link>>

:: Islander Elder Revisit
<<effects>><<wearProp "tea">>
<<loadNPC 0 "waterdragon_elder">><<person1>>
The same round room. The same brazier. The same tea that smells of brine and flowers. The Elder pours you a cup and sits opposite, as though you were merely a few minutes late for something the two of you had arranged.
<br><br>
"They still reach for you," <<he>> says. "I told you they might. I am sorry."
<br><br>
<<He>> watches you over the rim of <<his>> cup.
<br><br>
"Stay as long as you need. When you go, I will make sure the path out is clear."
<br><br>
<<link [[Rest, then go|Islander Elder Leave]]>><<pass 35>><</link>>

:: Islander Elder Leave
<<effects>><<wearProp "tea">>
You finish the tea. The Elder sees you to the door. The masked islanders outside bow their heads and make no move as you pass.
<br><br>
The corridor carries you gently out into the woods above the ruin, leaving the castle behind you as though it had quietly agreed to forget you were ever a prisoner in it.<<stress -8>><<tiredness -25>><<llstress>><<ltiredness>>
<br><br>
<<if !$island.home>>
	<<link [[Next|Island Treeline Search]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Island]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Water Dragon Helpers [widget]
<<widget "waterdragonTravelContinue">>
	<<if $waterdragonJourneyDay gte 7>>
		<<link [[Follow the pull (1:00)|Water Dragon Island Arrival 1]]>><<pass 60>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<<link [[Continue onward (1 day)|Water Dragon Island Travel Day]]>><<pass 1 day>><<set $waterdragonJourneyDay += 1>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "waterdragon_island_event_home">>
	You aren't quite sure why, but some deep part of you feels safe here, almost as if this island is home somehow. 
	The sensation is gentle rather than overwhelming, a warmth in your chest that softens some old, hard knot within you.<<lstress>><<stress -8>><<ltrauma>><<trauma -2>>
	<br><br>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Next|Island]]>><<endevent>><<island_explore_end>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "waterdragon_island_event_language">>
	<<generateRole 0 0 "islander">><<person1>>
	A lone <<person>> passes within sight of you, speaking to someone you can't see. The words remain incomprehensible, but something in their rhythm feels familiar enough to make your ears perk and your chest ache.
	<br><br>
	You wipe at your eyes, startled to realise tears have gathered there at all.<<gggcomprehension>><<islander_language 30>>
	<br><br>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Next|Island]]>><<endevent>><<island_explore_end>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "waterdragon_island_event_trill">>
	The smell of damp plants and salt-warmed flowers wraps around you while birdsong trickles overhead. Your tail gives a quiet swish behind you and an urge rises in your throat to answer the island back.
	<br><br>
	When you let the trill out, it feels embarrassingly natural. The surrounding birds go briefly still, then answer in a burst of noise from the wild.<<lstress>><<stress -6>>
	<br><br>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Next|Island]]>><<endevent>><<island_explore_end>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "waterdragon_island_event_tidepool">>
	In a tidepool sheltered among black stones, your reflection wavers with every ripple. Horns, ears, tail, altered eyes as if none of it looks strange here. 
	For a moment, under the island sky, your changed body feels less like a curse and more like an inheritance.
	<br><br>
	You stay there longer than you meant to, simply breathing.<<lstress>><<stress -5>><<gawareness>><<awareness 1>>
	<br><br>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Next|Island]]>><<endevent>><<island_explore_end>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "waterdragon_island_event_carving">>
	Half-buried stones jut from the earth in a curved line, worn by weather and roots. When your fingers brush the carvings cut into them, the lines feel deliberate.
	<br><br>
	You still can't read them, but they feel less alien than they should.<<ggcomprehension>><<islander_language 20>><<gawareness>><<awareness 1>>
	<br><br>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Next|Island]]>><<endevent>><<island_explore_end>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "waterdragon_island_event_spring">>
	You find a spring-fed pool hidden under ferns and leaning stone. The water is cool, clean, and sweet enough to make your whole body loosen when you drink and rinse the salt from your face. 
	<br><br>
	Along with it, some fish flash before you. Instinct takes over. You dart after them, body moving with sudden, easy precision, and snatch enough fish to quiet the ache in your belly before they scatter.<<lhunger>><<hunger -300>>
	<br><br>
	By the time you leave, the worst of the ache in your limbs has eased.<<set _springRest to Math.max(6, Math.floor(C.tiredness.max * 0.05))>><<set $tiredness = Math.clamp($tiredness - _springRest, 0, C.tiredness.max)>><<lstress>><<stress -4>><<ltrauma>><<trauma -1>>
	<br><br>
	<<icon "tf_waterdragon.png">><<link [[Next|Island]]>><<endevent>><<island_explore_end>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "waterdragon_island_event_blue_moon">>
	Beyond a curtain of hanging vines, a broken terrace opens out towards the sea. Shallow bowls have been carved into the stone with each one holding rainwater, a few fallen petals, pale shells arranged by hands that knew what they were doing.
	<br><br>
	Three moon marks curve around the largest bowl. One is pale, almost untouched. One has been stained blue with ground mineral. The third is cut deep and jagged, its old pigment dark as dried blood.
	<br><br>
	You run your fingers over the blue mark. The sky has nothing to do with it, yet your thoughts drift somewhere distant place of another moon. What comes back isn't quite a memory, more like the feeling of one: 
	food passed around in leaf-wrapped parcels, feet slapping wet stone, fish crackling over coals. Children shrieking. Adults dancing. The whole island given back in one night under the tide, reef, rain, fruit, everything.
	<br><br>
	You pull your hand away. How did you know that? Why would a dead celebration surface in your mind as though someone had once taught it to you?<<gawareness>><<awareness 1>>
	<br><br>
	<<tficon "waterdragon">><<link [[Next|Island]]>><<endevent>><<island_explore_end>><</link>>
<</widget>>
